    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Description\n\nIn `mini.pick` I would like the `choose` option to be triggered by both `<C-y>` (when navigating with `<C-n>` and `<C-p>`) or `<CR>` (when I fall directly on the match after typing).\n\nThe simplest way to set this up from a user perspective would probably be `require(\"mini.pick\").setup({ mappings = { choose = { \"<C-y>\", \"<CR>\" } })`, although I understand it might not be simple to implement.\n\nAnother possible workaround would be to add `<CR>` to the alternative mappings, but I guess this might be too constraining if one wants to use `<CR>` for something else.\n\nI looked at the existing issue and could see a similar discussion for `mini.files` (#534, #409, #1309, #879) with `MiniFilesBufferCreate`, but I could not find such an event for mini.pick, and in the code the mappings don't seem defined through regular `vim.keymap.set` for `mini.pick`.\n\nI'd be happy to try a PR if you think it could help.\n\nThank you!",
