            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nThis is already possible by creating [custom action](). Here is a longer (possibly more robust) version of having `<C-y>` choose the current item:\n\n```lua\nrequire('mini.pick').setup({\n  mappings = {\n    choose_2 = {\n      char = '<C-y>',\n      func = function()\n        local cur_item = MiniPick.get_picker_matches().current\n        local choose = MiniPick.get_picker_opts().source.choose\n        choose(cur_item)\n        return true\n      end,\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nAnd here is a shorter version that should work in at least 95% of setups:\n\n```lua\nrequire('mini.pick').setup({\n  mappings = {\n    choose_2 = { char = '<C-y>', func = function() vim.api.nvim_input('<CR>') end },\n  },\n})\n```",
